  <note><content><p>RK16 compares four methods with complete ordered outputs on 18 unique18 development records, preserving duplicate sequences at their original generation-call positions and evaluating dense AUC over B1–B10 plus normalized HV at B11.</p><p>LinearDesign achieves mean AUC 22.794606 and B11 HV 29.972887, versus 14.896234 and 16.693982 for EnsembleDesign-11, 5.205444 and 7.989211 for codonGPT, and 0.702952 and 0.966618 for uniform synonymous sampling.</p><p>Across 20,000 record-paired bootstraps, all six primary effects are positive, all 95% CIs exclude zero, every Holm-adjusted p-value is 0.00059997, and the LinearDesign-minus-EnsembleDesign effects are +7.898372 AUC and +13.278905 B11 HV.</p><p>Independent verification passed 88/88, finalization 53/53, manuscript verification 59/59, and the full CPU regression reported 347 passed and 1 skipped.</p><p>This surrogate-objective, common-generation-budget result is not time-matched and does not establish functional improvement, CodonFlow-RK superiority, full seven-method dense coverage, or external SOTA; functional OOD and untouched remain unevaluated, RK-G1 remains false, generator training remains unauthorized, and GEMORNA, the legacy LinearDesign scan, and CAI-greedy lack the required dense raw trajectories (source: commit 4115d281abe4a798b05525dff43f751460ee03a3, manuscript section 6.31).</p></content></note>
